<title>USA: Capital cuts EPS target to 5-10 pct higher.</title>
<headline>Capital cuts EPS target to 5-10 pct higher.</headline>
<dateline>FALLS CHURCH, Va. 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capital One Financial Corp said Tuesday it lowered its 1997 earnings forecast to five percent to 10 percent more than the $2.30 a share the bank reported in 1996.</p>
<p>A First Call estimate of 20 brokers put the company's 1997 earnings at $2.62 a share, or about 14 percent more than last year.</p>
<p>The bank said actual results for 1996 could be influnenced by the level of loans outstanding, delinquencies and charge-offs in the second half of the year.</p>
</text>
